course: dictionary
lesson: 14771
title: Protracted: lasting a long time
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Protracted is a long word, but you can break it into a simple idea. It means something lasts a long time, often longer than anyone expected or wanted. «After a protracted wait, the bus finally arrived.» The wait was long, and it felt too long, so protracted means long and drawn out.
explain: Protracted is also the past form of the verb protract, which means to make something last longer. «The meeting was protracted by arguments.» Here the arguments made the meeting last longer. Read the words around the word to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Protracted sounds like protractor, the tool you use in maths to measure angles. They come from the same root, which means drawing out, but a protractor is a different word with a different meaning. Check the sentence: does it talk about time or measuring?
fact: Protracted means lasting a long time, often longer than expected or wanted.
fact: Protracted is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as «a protracted illness».
fact: Protract is a verb meaning to make something last longer, and protracted is its past form.
fact: In news and formal writing, you might read about «protracted talks», «a protracted war» or «protracted negotiations».
fact: A protractor is a maths tool for measuring angles. It is a different word, even though it comes from the same root.
exercise: «After a protracted wait, the bus finally arrived.» What does protracted mean? | Very cold | Broken down | Very fast | *Lasting a long time
exercise: «The protracted war lasted for ten years.» How long did the war last? | Ten minutes | Ten days | *Ten years | Ten hours
exercise: Ella's maths teacher hands out protractors. What does a protractor measure? | Time | Distance | Weight | *Angles
test: «His protracted illness kept him off school for most of the term.» What does protracted mean here? | Very loud | *Lasting a long time, longer than wanted | Quick and sudden | Happy and bright
test: «The meeting was protracted by arguments.» Here protracted is the past form of protract. What does it mean? | *Made to last longer than it should | Cancelled | Moved to a new room | Finished early
exam: «The negotiations were protracted, and both sides were tired of arguing.» Which description fits the negotiations best? | *Long and drawn out | Cheap and simple | Short and friendly | Secret and quick
